module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.closed_variant_partition_read_as_a_default_arm

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

data closed_variant_partition_read_as_a_default_arm: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "closed_variant_partition_read_as_a_default_arm" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "closed variant partition read as a default arm (a selector over a CLOSED coproduct tests some of its variants by name and treats every other reading as the remaining one, so a reading that matches nothing renders a plausible arm instead of refusing; the coproduct's exhaustiveness is asserted in prose and lost at the string boundary where the variant name is read back off the source)",
    "INSTANCE, 2026-09-10, in the emitter's compiler-entry arm selection. std.compiler_entry declares exactly three drivers (RetainedHostCliKernel, DirectIngestDriver, SourceRootEvalDriver). v1.compiler.emit_rust emit_main_rs asked compiler_pipeline_entry_is_retained_host, then compiler_pipeline_entry_is_source_root_eval, then RETURNED THE DIRECT-INGEST MAIN unconditionally. Both predicates compare a String read back out of the declaration body (authored_name_at over the item's source span), so the third arm was not a variant match at all: it was the residue of two string comparisons.",
    "WHAT WAS OBSERVED, and it is a silent wrong answer rather than a low rung (DESIGN section 5). Emitting src/v2/compiler/00_compile.dag — whose declaration reads `data compiler_pipeline_entry: CompilerEntryDriver = SourceRootEvalDriver` — at a 404-module import closure rendered the DIRECT-INGEST main: a 25-line main that reads one source path and translates it. The same emission rendered `compiler_pipeline_entry() -> CompilerEntryDriver::SourceRootEvalDriver` into the same crate, so the emitted VALUE and the emitted ENTRY POINT disagreed inside one artifact, with zero diagnostics of any severity. The crate compiles; the binary runs; it answers a different question than the lane that spawns it asks.",
    "THE SUBJECT IS THE READING, NOT THE CLOSURE SIZE, and the cheap reproducer is what establishes that. `fixtures/unknown_pipeline_driver/probe.dag` declares `compiler_pipeline_entry: CompilerEntryDriver = std.compiler_entry.SourceRootEvalDriver` -- an ORDINARY ACCEPTED PROGRAM, spelled with its declaring module's qualifier, which resolves to the variant it names. At SEVENTEEN modules the pre-fix emitter rendered the DIRECT-INGEST main for it, with zero diagnostics of any severity. The 404-module observation that surfaced the class is therefore an instance and not the subject: any reading the span-read cannot match by bare name selects the residue arm, and a qualified spelling is the smallest such reading.",
    "THE FIRST OBSERVATION, kept because it is what made the class visible and because it shows the damage in production shape. Emitting `src/v2/compiler/00_compile.dag` at a 404-module import closure rendered the direct-ingest main while the SAME emission rendered `compiler_pipeline_entry() -> CompilerEntryDriver::SourceRootEvalDriver` into the same crate -- the emitted VALUE and the emitted ENTRY POINT disagreeing inside one artifact. The identical entry renders the eval-driver main at 173 and 177 modules. Shrinking that closure back to 183 restored the correct arm, which is why the closure split MUST NOT be read as the fix: it moved the corpus off the defect, it did not remove it.",
    "THE REPAIR IS THE PARTITION CLOSED BY NAME. compiler_pipeline_entry_driver_is_known tests the reading against all three declared drivers and emit_main_rs refuses first, rendering a compile_error that names the module and the reading it got, so an unrecognised reading stops the line instead of selecting an arm. That wall is executed by `v1.compiler.tests` `unknown_pipeline_driver_refusal_test`, whose fixture is the accepted program above and whose red control is the pre-fix direct-ingest shape, so the rung is mitigation WITH executed evidence rather than a declared one; the CEILING is higher and the trigger is nameable: the driver is a CLOSED coproduct, so an emitter that matched the resolved variant rather than a string read back off the source span could not express this state at all. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: emit_main_rs selects on the resolved CompilerEntryDriver variant (an exhaustive match the emitter cannot compile with an arm missing) instead of on authored_name_at of the declaration body.",
    "THE REVIEW TELL, general to the class: a selector whose last arm is reached by `else` / `return` rather than by naming its variant, over a type whose declaration is a closed coproduct. Ask what the selector does when the discriminator reads as NONE of the names — if the answer is 'the last arm', the exhaustiveness the type carries has been dropped at that boundary.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.emit_rust", decl_name: "compiler_pipeline_entry_driver_is_known", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.emit_rust", decl_name: "emit_unknown_compiler_pipeline_driver_main_rs", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.compiler_entry", decl_name: "CompilerEntryDriver", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
